model.en:
async listAuthorsWithCounts() {
  // load the relation explicitly FOR THIS QUERY -> one LEFT JOIN, one round trip
  const authors = await this.repo.find({ relations: { posts: true } });
  return authors.map((a) => ({
    name: a.name,
    postCount: a.posts.length,   // already loaded, no await, no extra query
  }));
}

// QueryBuilder variant when you need columns / WHERE / pagination:
//   this.repo.createQueryBuilder('author')
//     .leftJoinAndSelect('author.posts', 'post')
//     .getMany();

Why: find({ relations: { posts: true } }) tells TypeORM to LEFT JOIN posts in the same statement, so parents and children come back in one round trip regardless of list size. The per-author `await a.posts` is gone, so there is no per-row query. For 100 authors this is 1 query instead of 101. The loading decision is now explicit and visible at the call site, and trivially removable on paths that don't need posts.

